    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are prioritizing high-upside speed and favorable matchups today, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.24), our strongest start. Facing Luis Castillo, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite platoon advantage and the aggressive base-running environment we prioritize, making him a prime candidate to anchor our stolen base category despite the moderate opposing xERA. We are also leaning heavily into **Trea Turner** (73.19), **Kyle Schwarber** (72.52), and **Junior Caminero** (72.15). The latter enjoys a soft matchup against Brandon Young, while **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** capitalize on a prime opportunity against Junk, where their high order placement significantly boosts their daily efficiency scores. **Caleb Durbin** also projects as a strong play (69.02), as his matchup against Mitch Bratt allows us to exploit a clear platoon edge and a favorable SP xERA of 5.58.\n\nThe decision to keep **Pedro Ramirez** (50.32) on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning; he sits just outside our optimal configuration primarily due to the defensive and situational depth provided by **Colt Keith** (61.53), who fits better into the utility spot given the current roster construction and the objective to prioritize specific categories. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Hector Rodriguez** (56.40), who, despite a solid projection, carries a 32% rain risk that could compromise his total output. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (55.47), **Chase Meidroth** (55.14), and **Carson Benge** (55.18) are currently in the lineup, we are monitoring their status closely as the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Lars Nootbaar** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** mean their anticipated batting orders\u2014and thus their projected scores\u2014remain subject to volatility. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** all sidelined by scheduled days off, we are relying on the secondary depth of **Dillon Dingler** (45.61) to hold the floor while the high-speed anchors carry the load.",
